# How to Package and Run the Project on a New Laptop

To move this system from this computer to another laptop and get it running perfectly, you only need to follow these simple steps.

---

## Part 1: Packaging the Project (On This Computer)

1. Navigate to the `Videos` folder on this computer.
2. Locate the folder named **`mattews`**.
3. Right-click the **`mattews`** folder and select **Compress to ZIP file** (or "Send to > Compressed (zipped) folder").
4. Copy the newly created `mattews.zip` file onto a USB Flash Drive (or email/Google Drive it to the new laptop).

---

## Part 2: Preparing the New Laptop

Before the code can run, the new laptop needs the core engine (Python).

1. On the new laptop, download and install **Python** from [python.org/downloads](https://www.python.org/downloads/).
2. **⚠️ CRITICAL STEP DURING INSTALLATION:** When the Python installer opens, look at the very bottom of the window and check the box that says **"Add python.exe to PATH"**. If you skip this, the project will not run. Then click "Install Now".

---

## Part 3: Running the Project (On the New Laptop)

1. Move the `mattews.zip` file from your USB drive to the new laptop (e.g., to the Desktop or Documents folder).
2. Right-click the zip file and select **Extract All...** to unzip it.
3. Open the newly unzipped **`mattews`** folder.
4. Click firmly inside the **Address Bar** at the top of the folder window (where it says the folder path, like `C:\Users\Name\Desktop\mattews`).
5. Delete whatever is in the address bar, type **`cmd`**, and press **Enter**.
   *This will open a black terminal window pointing exactly at your project folder.*

### Installing the Brains (One-Time Setup)
Your project needs certain libraries (like Streamlit and Scikit-Learn) to function. In the black terminal window, copy and paste this command and press Enter:
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
*(Wait 1-2 minutes for it to download everything. You only ever have to do this once.)*

### Launching the Dashboard
Finally, to start the website, type this into the terminal and press Enter:
```bash
python -m streamlit run app.py
```

The web browser on the new laptop will automatically open, and the Kitale National Polytechnic dashboard will be up and running!
